  "summary": {
    "totalLayers": 10,
    "primaryLanguages": ["Julia", "C", "C++", "Scheme"],
    "architecture": "Layered: Runtime (C/C++) -> Support -> CLI -> Compiler/Parser/Lowering (Julia) -> Base -> Stdlib -> Docs/Tests/Build",
    "notes": "Julia uses a unique architecture where the compiler, parser, and lowering are written in Julia itself (bootstrapped). The C/C++ runtime provides the execution substrate. Base library is the minimal core loaded at startup; stdlib packages are optional add-ons."
